            crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "a kind of hardwood (perhaps boxwood), used by turners, especially for handles of knives, daggers etc.; the hilt of a dagger made from this wood (OED s.v. dudgeon n.1) | a kind of hardwood (perhaps boxwood), u.a. used by turners, especially for handles of knives, daggers etc.; the hilt of a dagger made from this wood (OED s.v. dudgeon n.1) | a kind of hardwood (perhaps boxwood), among other things used by turners, especially for handles of knives, daggers etc.; the hilt of a dagger made from this wood (OED s.v. dudgeon n.1) | a kind of hardwood (perhaps boxwood), used by turners, especially for handles of knives, daggers etc. (OED s.v. dudgeon n.1) | a kind of hardwood (perhaps boxwood), u.a. used by turners, especially for handles of knives, daggers etc. (OED s.v. dudgeon n.1) | (dougeon) a kind of hardwood (perhaps boxwood), u.a. used by turners, especially for handles of knives, daggers etc.; the hilt of a dagger made from this wood (OED s.v. dudgeon n.^1) | a kind of hardwood (perhaps boxwood), among other things used by turners, especially for handles of knives, daggers etc. (OED s.v. dudgeon n.1) | a kind of hardwood (perhaps boxwood), u.a. used by turners, especially for handles of knives, daggers etc. (OED s.v. dudgeon n.^1) | a kind of hardwood (perhaps boxwood), used by turners, esp. for handles of knives, daggers etc.; the hilt of a dagger made from this wood (OED s.v. dudgeon n.1)" ;
